---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";

// The owner wants this page to match their supplied draft word for word, so
// the copy is verbatim and nothing here adapts to CMS settings.
const updated = "9 October 2026";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="What GrintByte collects when you use this site, why, and how to reach us about it."
>
  <article class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-12 sm:py-16">
    <h1 class="text-3xl font-extrabold tracking-tight sm:text-4xl">Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-ink-soft">Last updated: {updated}</p>

    <div class="prose-grint mt-8 space-y-8 text-base leading-relaxed">
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold">The Short Version</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">
          This site collects as little data as possible. We do not use third-party advertising
          trackers, we do not set tracking cookies, and nothing is sold or shared for marketing
          purposes. The personal information we receive is limited to what you provide through our
          contact forms or when purchasing software licenses, used solely to support you and
          deliver your digital products.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold">Purchases and Payments</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">
          All product order processing, payment collection, and digital delivery are handled
          directly by our Merchant of Record, <em>Lemon Squeezy</em> (Lemon Squeezy, LLC).
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3">
          Your sensitive payment information (such as credit card numbers or billing details) is
          submitted directly to Lemon Squeezy and never passes through or gets stored on our
          servers. Lemon Squeezy securely processes transactions and provides us only with the
          operational data required to deliver and manage your digital software licenses (such as
          your name, email address, order reference number, and items purchased). For more details,
          please review
          the <a href="https://www.lemonsqueezy.com/privacy" rel="noopener" class="text-brand underline">Lemon Squeezy Privacy Policy</a>.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold">The Contact Form</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">
          When you submit an enquiry, we collect your name, email address, optional company name,
          and message strictly to assist you and respond to your questions. Your message is
          forwarded to our team and recorded securely on our administrative cloud systems to ensure
          proper follow-up. We never add your contact information to marketing or newsletter lists
          without your explicit opt-in consent.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold">Hosting and Server Logs</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">
          This website is hosted using third-party cloud infrastructure. When you browse our
          website, hosting servers may automatically record standard access logs. This technical
          data can include your IP address, browser type, operating system, referring URL, and the
          date/time of access. These logs are used strictly for technical performance diagnostics,
          network stability, and security monitoring, and are not combined with any personally
          identifiable information.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold">Data Retention and Your Rights</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">
          We retain customer correspondence and support enquiries only for as long as necessary to
          address your requests, manage product license renewals, and fulfill administrative or
          legal obligations.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3">
          If you would like to know what information we hold about you or request its deletion,
          please contact us
          at <em><a href="mailto:team@grintbyte.com" class="text-brand underline">team@grintbyte.com</a></em> (or <a href="mailto:grintbyte@gmail.com" class="text-brand underline">grintbyte@gmail.com</a>),
          and we will fulfill your request promptly. Any updates to this policy will be posted on
          this page with a revised date at the top.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
